Dear Hiring Team,

I am applying for the Core Services Software Developer - Network role. I am drawn to this role because it combines the systems work I enjoy most with the opportunity to build foundational software for Apple's global network.

At Moloco, I learned to treat infrastructure as a product for the engineers who depend on it. Working on production systems taught me that safe rollouts, clear behavior during failures, and efficient resource use are as important as feature delivery. I collaborated with product and infrastructure teams to make those systems useful and dependable across the organization. This experience made me comfortable taking ownership in ambiguous environments, diagnosing problems across service boundaries, and improving the operational experience for other engineers.

My computer science background has given me a strong foundation in operating systems, networking, databases, and security. Beyond coursework, I extended the Linux DRM scheduler with an EEVDF-inspired algorithm to improve interactive tail latency and implemented a trap-and-emulate hypervisor on OpenSBI. These projects strengthened how I reason about scheduling, isolation, performance, and failure boundaries. I would bring that systems-oriented approach and my foundation in networking to building reliable and scalable tools for Apple's core network.

Thank you for your consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my production infrastructure experience and systems background could contribute to the team.

#v(12pt)

